pi-lsp — vendored bundled extension
===================================

Upstream package : @narumitw/pi-lsp 0.49.9 (MIT)
Upstream author  : narumiruna (https://github.com/narumiruna/pi-extensions)
License          : MIT — see LICENSE (copied verbatim from upstream)

This directory is OMA's bundled copy of the pi-lsp extension:

  upstream/        exact npm tarball content of @narumitw/pi-lsp@0.49.9,
                   unmodified — the integrity-pinned source snapshot.
  upstream-tests/  the upstream test tree from the source commit named in
                   manifest.json (the npm tarball does not ship tests);
                   vendored so OMA's ported boundary tests can cite and
                   re-derive upstream's fixtures.
  runtime/         tsc-compiled JavaScript + declarations of upstream's
                   library modules, generated by scripts/vendor-pi-lsp.mjs
                   from upstream/src. Generated, hash-pinned inputs — not
                   authored OMA code. Upstream's Pi entry files
                   (index.ts, pi-lsp.ts) are vendored for provenance but
                   are never loaded: OMA registers its own tool adapter
                   (src/extension/lsp-tools.ts), which keeps process,
                   workspace, environment and mutation authority in OMA.
  manifest.json    generated bundle manifest: per-file SHA-256, byte
                   counts and a deterministic whole-bundle digest, plus
                   the upstream name/version/commit and npm tarball
                   integrity/shasum metadata.

No part of this bundle is fetched, installed or cloned at run time.
